// RFC-0031 §S7–§S8 — organic fusion (metaball / blob merging).
//
// Run it (from the repo root):
//   cd crates/byard-cli/examples/organic_fusion
//   cargo run -p byard-cli -- dev
//
// `fuse: <px>` is the smoothing radius: the distance over which two surfaces
// bridge into one. It is a polynomial smooth-minimum over the group's members,
// and the blend factor that produced the geometry is the same one that mixes
// their colours — so the surface bridge and the colour transition are one
// event, which is what makes differently-coloured fusion read as deliberate.
//
// `fuse: 0`, and an absent `fuse`, are exactly today's behaviour: each shape is
// its own instance, unchanged.
//
// What to look for:
//   1. The k ramp: the same three circles at four smoothing radii. At 0 they
//      are three discs; by 28 they are one body with no seam.
//   2. The approach: a circle sliding towards a fixed one. Far apart, nothing
//      happens — fusion is local. As it arrives, a bridge grows between them
//      *before* the shapes touch, and the colours cross it.
//   3. The fused outline: a stroked group is the boundary of the union, not a
//      union of the members' outlines. There are no seams through the interior,
//      which is the whole reason to fuse in the first place.
//   4. Fusion composes with everything else the pipeline does: these are
//      `ngon`s, and the whole group carries a paint-time transform.
//
// Two things the compiler will tell you about, and why:
//   - a fused group has one outline, drawn from the *first* shape's stroke.
//     A `stroke:` on a later shape is a **warning**: the property is inert, the
//     shape still renders correctly, and so it does not fail the build.
//   - `dash:` on a fused stroke is an **error**: there is no arc length along
//     the union of two shapes, and an approximation would make the dashes crawl
//     as the fusion changes.
View Main() {
    Column #[bg: 0x14161C, p: 32, gap: 26, width: 760] {
        Text("fuse — surfaces that bridge, and colours that cross the bridge")
            #[color: 0xF2F3F5, size: 20, weight: bold]

        // ── 1. The smoothing radius ──────────────────────────────────────
        Text("the same three circles at fuse 0, 10, 20, 28")
            #[color: 0x8A90A0, size: 13]
        Row #[gap: 12] {
            Canvas #[width: 168, height: 96, bg: 0x1C1F27, fuse: 0] {
                circle(cx: 46, cy: 48, r: 22, fill: 0x5B8DEF)
                circle(cx: 90, cy: 48, r: 18, fill: 0x4CC38A)
                circle(cx: 128, cy: 48, r: 14, fill: 0xE8B54A)
            }
            Canvas #[width: 168, height: 96, bg: 0x1C1F27, fuse: 10] {
                circle(cx: 46, cy: 48, r: 22, fill: 0x5B8DEF)
                circle(cx: 90, cy: 48, r: 18, fill: 0x4CC38A)
                circle(cx: 128, cy: 48, r: 14, fill: 0xE8B54A)
            }
            Canvas #[width: 168, height: 96, bg: 0x1C1F27, fuse: 20] {
                circle(cx: 46, cy: 48, r: 22, fill: 0x5B8DEF)
                circle(cx: 90, cy: 48, r: 18, fill: 0x4CC38A)
                circle(cx: 128, cy: 48, r: 14, fill: 0xE8B54A)
            }
            Canvas #[width: 168, height: 96, bg: 0x1C1F27, fuse: 28] {
                circle(cx: 46, cy: 48, r: 22, fill: 0x5B8DEF)
                circle(cx: 90, cy: 48, r: 18, fill: 0x4CC38A)
                circle(cx: 128, cy: 48, r: 14, fill: 0xE8B54A)
            }
        }

        // ── 2. The approach: an animated member, a static smoothing radius ─
        //
        // Note that it is the *member* that moves here, not the head. That is
        // the case RFC-0031's INV-26 exists for: the head's own bytes never
        // change, and without the member hash folded into it the group would be
        // judged clean and would paint last frame's shape forever.
        Text("an approaching member — fusion is local, and the bridge grows before contact")
            #[color: 0x8A90A0, size: 13]
        Canvas #[width: 340, height: 110, bg: 0x1C1F27, fuse: 22] {
            circle(cx: 70, cy: 55, r: 26, fill: 0x5B8DEF)
            circle(cx: 250 with anim.ease_in_out(1800ms, from: 130,
                                                 repeat: infinite, reverse: true),
                   cy: 55, r: 20, fill: 0xE8734A)
        }

        Row #[gap: 20] {
            // ── 3. The fused outline is the union's boundary ─────────────
            Column #[gap: 10] {
                Text("a stroked group: one outline, no seams")
                    #[color: 0x8A90A0, size: 13]
                Canvas #[width: 220, height: 120, bg: 0x1C1F27, fuse: 18] {
                    // The first shape's stroke is the *group's* outline.
                    circle(cx: 80, cy: 60, r: 34, stroke: 0xE6E1E5, stroke_width: 3)
                    circle(cx: 140, cy: 60, r: 28)
                }
            }

            // ── 4. It composes ──────────────────────────────────────────
            Column #[gap: 10] {
                Text("ngons, fused, under a paint-time transform")
                    #[color: 0x8A90A0, size: 13]
                Box #[rotate: 8deg, scale: (0.95, 0.95)] {
                    Canvas #[width: 220, height: 120, bg: 0x1C1F27, fuse: 24] {
                        ngon(cx: 78, cy: 60, r: 32, n: 6, corner: 6, fill: 0x4CC38A)
                        ngon(cx: 140, cy: 60, r: 28, n: 5, corner: 4, inner: 0.6,
                             fill: 0xE8B54A)
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
